  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A mass-spring system and a simple pendulum both oscillate with period <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"T\"></span>. The mass on the spring and the mass of the pendulum bob are both initially <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1\"></span> kg. What is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{time\\: period\\: of\\: the\\: mass-spring\\: system}{time\\: period\\: of\\: the\\: simple\\: pendulum}\"></span> when the mass on the spring and the mass of the pendulum bob are both increased to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2\"></span> kg?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{2}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\sqrt{2}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
  },
